WEBVTT

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:07.110
<b>Class 5-2</b>

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.770
Itsumo-san!

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:10.940
Wanna hang out with us
on the way home?

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.130
Sorry, I have to help out at home.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:15.850
Oh, is that so?

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:17.660
Some other time, then.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:18.820
Let's go!

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.370
Where should we go?

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.370
How about the park?

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:36.150
Sounds good. Let's go.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:37.500
What do you wanna play?

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:38.470
Let's jump rope!

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.100
Nice! That's it!

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:46.710
Thank you very much.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.470
Are you all right?

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.320
Did you get hurt?

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:00.120
I'm sorry. I knocked over some stuff.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.680
It's no problem. I'll clean this up.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:03.700
Sorry again.

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:49.170
<b>Scorching</b>

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:49.170
<b>Ping Pong Girls</b>

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:55.820
<b>Sixth Serve</b>

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:55.820
<b>Friends</b>

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:00.350
Okay, here we go.

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:00.950
Right!

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:04.970
Come on, girls!
That practice match is next week!

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:07.490
Put your heart into practice!

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:08.450
Yes!

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:19.720
Are you looking down on me?

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.210
This is weird.
It doesn't make any sense.

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:27.110
And it's not just today.
Something's been off with you lately.

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:29.270
Your smashes have clearly gotten worse!

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:33.230
They were way more lethal
when we first played!

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:38.360
Yeah, I've had trouble
nailing smashes right lately.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:40.320
I knew it!

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:43.350
What's gotten into you?
The practice match is coming up!

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:45.600
Are you sick or something?

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:46.590
Is it a cold?

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:50.330
This is why I told you so many times
to cover your belly while sleeping!

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.090
I'm fine!

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:55.210
Though I did sleep
with my belly exposed.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.460
Then why are you in such bad shape?

00:03:57.990 --> 00:03:59.210
It's the rubber.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:01.900
H-Hokuto-san?

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:06.670
If there's nothing wrong with your body,
then it's probably the racket.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.180
Let me see it.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:14.880
There's a white spot on the surface.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:18.940
And it's so smooth,
it's not even getting stuck in my hair.

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:20.840
There's no doubt about it.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:24.280
You're not playing well because
your rubber's at the end of its lifespan.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:26.360
Oh, I see.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:27.630
Agari-senpai.

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:29.740
What's this about the rubber's lifespan?

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:34.790
You know how table tennis rackets
have a layer of rubber on each side?

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:38.650
These rubbers gradually
deteriorate with use,

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:43.380
reducing the speed of your strokes,
making it harder to impart spin on the ball,

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.990
and generally having
a negative impact on your game.

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:50.010
That's why you have to replace them
at regular intervals.

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:55.110
Judging from the extent of the wear,
she's probably used it for about two months.

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:58.810
It must be replaced
with a new rubber immediately.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:01.070
Yeah, it has been two months.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:03.400
Wow! How'd you know?

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:06.660
Because Hokuto's family runs
a table tennis store!

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:10.850
She's seen thousands of rubbers!

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:14.340
Figuring out how long one's been used
is a piece of cake for her.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.000
Stop squeezing.

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:20.800
Rubbers are a treasure trove of information.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:23.980
The type, combination,
and wear of a player's rubber

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:30.030
reveal everything about
its user's play style, best moves,

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:31.660
even their personality...

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:35.350
And, of course, the color of their panties.

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:40.470
Pink.

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:45.440
I see. So I'd better buy some new rubber.

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:50.490
If it's rubbers you want,
we're the store for you.

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:54.320
We're waiting for you with a huge
and varied collection, Peach Panties.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.860
And I'll give you a special
teammate discount, Peach Panties.

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:00.290
Please stop referring to her
by the color of her panties.

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:02.630
Oh, but...

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:07.100
I've used up my allowance.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:08.760
I'm broke now.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.650
Beam, beam...

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:12.840
Y-You see,

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:17.170
I got hooked on collecting
the Cosplay Puppy mascot series.

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:20.380
And before I knew it, I'd run out of money.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:22.560
Good day, Thong-senpai.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:25.950
I have here table tennis shoes
that are the perfect size for you.

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:27.020
How about a pair?

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:29.320
Call me Munemune-senpai!

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:31.730
She's suddenly acting so distant!

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:35.220
I'm not interested in Peach Panties
that won't make me any money.

00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:38.410
Ever the money-monger, I see.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.810
Then, how about you help out at her store

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:44.670
and buy new rubbers with the money?

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:48.880
Don't you always say
you're understaffed?

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:53.140
That will be 8,376 yen.

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:57.140
Here's your 124 yen in change.

00:06:57.720 --> 00:06:59.730
Thank you very much!

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:06.230
Come on, Taily! You can't do anything
if you're just hiding all the time!

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:08.940
But it's so embarrassing!

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:10.970
I need your help, Hanabi.

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:13.780
Coming right up, Hokuto.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:15.650
Sorry, and thanks.

00:07:15.650 --> 00:07:18.360
Don't mention it!
We're friends, aren't we?

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:19.620
Beam, beam.

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:23.360
U-Um, don't tell me
you're leaving me alone here.

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:26.230
You can at least watch the store, right,

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:27.340
Peach Panties?

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:30.510
Yes...

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:35.390
<i>Y-Yeah. I need to do my job.</i>

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:39.700
<i>Hokuto-san's so graciously
letting me work here.</i>

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:43.850
<i>I-I have to do my best and be useful!</i>

00:07:44.570 --> 00:07:46.310
I'll take this.

00:07:46.310 --> 00:07:47.320
S-Sure!

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:56.670
Uh... Th-That'll be 2,652 yen.

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:57.640
Here.

00:07:57.640 --> 00:08:01.920
Th-Thank you! That's 3,000 yen.

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:08.800
H-Here's your 348 yen in change.

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:13.710
Th-Thank y-you...

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:16.220
Th-Thank you very much!

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:20.870
You're bowing too hard.

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:23.310
Your body's so flexible, Taily.

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:27.800
Also, when dealing with a customer,
you have to look them in the eye.

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:31.070
I get nervous in front of strangers!

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.570
Relax, relax.

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:35.530
Chill out a little.

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:38.240
It's not that easy.

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:43.710
Take some deep breaths
and calm down, then.

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:50.670
I'm not pregnant!

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:53.520
There's no substitute for experience.

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:55.650
You'll get used to it
as you handle them,

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:57.470
so hang in there,
Peach Panties.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:00.080
Please, stop calling me
by the color of my panties.

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:03.410
<i>Experience, huh?</i>

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:07.480
<i>Yeah, even in table tennis,
practicing loads helps you get better.</i>

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.940
<i>It's embarrassing,
but I'll have to deal with it!</i>

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:41.390
If you could bill me,
it'd please me to death.

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:46.310
S-Sure!

00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:51.550
<i>C-Calm down. Calm down.</i>

00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:52.850
<i>I can do this.</i>

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:54.280
<i>I can do this!</i>

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:57.150
Relax, relax.

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:20.970
Would you be so deathly kind
as to do me a favor?

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:30.460
What happened to Agari-senpai?

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:32.860
She lost another dare match.

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.860
Meowha.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:38.000
Why so fidgety?
Need to use the bathroom?

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.820
N-No!

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:42.290
You're worried about Koyori-chan, right?

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:44.500
Worried? Not at all!

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:47.580
Koyori's a total dimwit
outside of table tennis,

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.790
so I'm hoping she
isn't causing anyone trouble.

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:53.450
Maybe she's bowing impossibly hard

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:56.670
or having trouble
looking people in the eye!

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:58.720
Meow.

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:00.490
Wh-What is it?

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:01.770
Nothing...

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:04.960
We just thought you may as well ask
if you're that worried.

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:07.220
Like I said, I'm not worried!

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:10.140
Hello?

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:11.820
Hey, there.

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:13.900
How's Koyori-chan doing?

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:17.610
Oh, she's trying her best,
but she's stiff as heck.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:19.450
Apparently, she's stiff as heck.

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:20.660
I knew it!

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:25.220
I get that you're worried,
but focus on practice.

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:29.080
Our opponents next week are Mozuyama,
a team that went to Nationals.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:34.140
We'll only produce a boring result
if we don't take them on at our best.

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:37.990
What's more, that school has

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:41.220
one of the Elite Four Drivers like you,

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:44.140
the Driver of the East.

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:52.140
<b>1 point for every 1,000 yen spent!</b>

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:52.140
<b>Name:</b>

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:52.140
Futamaru

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:49.110
I risked death to collect 30 points,

00:11:49.110 --> 00:11:52.140
so I'd like to exchange them
for a bunny T-shirt.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:57.900
<b>Usa Mimi Table Tennis
Point Campaign</b>

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:57.900
<b>Collect our
original goods!</b>

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:57.900
10 Points 
Bunny Hand Towel

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:57.900
20 Points 
Bunny Ear Swab

00:11:56.230 --> 00:12:00.070
30 Points 
Bunny T-Shirt

00:11:56.230 --> 00:12:00.070
1,000 Points 
Bunny Hoodie

00:11:56.640 --> 00:11:59.050
O-Of course! One moment please!

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:04.030
W-Will this do?

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:07.930
This is it!

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:15.290
This fluffy tail is so incredibly,
deathly cute!

00:12:17.690 --> 00:12:21.430
Will this make her happy?

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:23.590
Will she accept it?

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:28.430
The friendship fee for this week...

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:33.290
I'm deathly sure this will do!

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:38.610
Th-Thank you very much!

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:47.370
<i>Wh-What was with that girl?</i>

00:12:57.330 --> 00:12:59.250
Let's get to work!

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:08.070
You seem used to this, Hana-chan.

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:10.120
Have you been helping out here long?

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:13.550
Yeah, fairly long.

00:13:13.550 --> 00:13:15.590
Come help, Hanabi.

00:13:15.590 --> 00:13:16.770
Sure!

00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:19.050
Get me that thing, Hanabi.

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:20.770
Here, rubber film.

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:22.000
The other thing, too.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.570
Oh, cleaner?

00:13:23.970 --> 00:13:26.070
Take care of that too, Hanabi.

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:28.780
Filing the receipts? Sure thing!

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:31.530
<i>She's in perfect sync with Hokuto-san!</i>

00:13:31.530 --> 00:13:33.250
<i>How does she actually know what to do?</i>

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:35.450
Leave the squeezing to me, too!

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:37.460
That, you don't have to do.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:40.460
Sorry for always making you do this.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:43.420
Don't mention it!
We're friends, aren't we?

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:48.360
Take care of that, too, Hanabi.

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:49.620
Got it!

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:52.970
You're amazing, Hana-chan!

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:54.910
I guess.

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:58.190
But I've got nothing on
Hokuto's working game.

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:02.320
Excuse me. I'd like to buy some rubber.

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:03.020
Sure.

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:06.170
What kind of rubber are you looking for?

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:08.210
I want to put spin on the ball.

00:14:08.210 --> 00:14:10.410
I want to turn it square!

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:15.500
In that case, how about this tacky rubber?

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:17.290
<b>Hokuto's</b>

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:17.290
<b>Rubber Lecture</b>

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:17.290
<b>Live</b>

00:14:18.140 --> 00:14:20.230
Unlike a regular rubber,

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:24.080
you can do this.

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:34.140
Tacky 
Rubber {left}

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:34.140
Regular 
Rubber {right}

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:27.400
The ball stuck to the racket!

00:14:27.960 --> 00:14:31.720
It'll suck in the ball using
its high friction and adhesion,

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:34.140
letting you impart more spin on the ball.

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:37.540
Wow! I'll take that rubber, please!

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:38.850
Thank you.

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:43.400
I'd like a rubber that'll
let me hit awesome winners!

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:48.860
If you want power, then I recommend
springy, high-tension rubber.

00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:50.570
I'll take it!

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:56.860
I've been stuck in a rut lately,
so I'd like to change up my play style.

00:14:56.860 --> 00:14:57.910
In that case,

00:14:59.020 --> 00:15:03.710
how about a long pips-out rubber,
with a unique, pimply texture?

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:06.580
Learning how to use it will be difficult,

00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:09.750
but if you do, you'll be able
to enjoy some unusual play.

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:10.970
I'll take it!

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:13.430
By combining it with a rubber
that makes it easy to apply spin...

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:17.760
Different types of rubbers
have completely different effects,

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:22.410
but since there are hundreds of types,
it's so hard to choose!

00:15:22.410 --> 00:15:23.400
Yeah, yeah!

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:25.760
But since Hokuto understands all of them,

00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:28.950
she can recommend
the perfect rubber for each customer.

00:15:28.950 --> 00:15:31.580
That's what makes her so awesome.

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:34.370
<b>Super Attendant
 Hokuto-san</b>

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:34.370
As for me...

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:35.410
<b>Hanabi's</b>

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:35.410
<b>Rubber Replacement Lecture</b>

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:35.410
<b>Live</b>

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:38.290
I'm an expert at gluing
and replacing rubber!

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:46.470
I can perfectly glue as many as you want!

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:47.250
Wow!

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.300
They're both amazing!

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:51.050
All right!

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:54.520
<i>I can't be outdone.</i>

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:55.810
<i>I'll do my best, too!</i>

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:04.800
Thank you very much!

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:17.580
Welcome...

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:21.580
Hey, there. How you doin'?

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:22.960
Thanks for having us.

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:24.890
The whole club's here!

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:25.670
Agari-chan!

00:16:26.060 --> 00:16:27.690
We're here.

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:29.840
Welcome!

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:31.990
What are you here for?

00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:34.520
To mess with you.

00:16:34.520 --> 00:16:35.930
Please leave.

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:42.630
You see, Agari-chan said she was
unbearably worried about Koyori-chan.

00:16:42.630 --> 00:16:43.980
Oh, it's fine, then.

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:46.690
Agari-chan!

00:16:47.090 --> 00:16:48.650
I-I didn't say that!

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:51.050
I never said anything like that!

00:16:51.050 --> 00:16:53.650
I just, uh,

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:57.040
c-came here to buy something!

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:59.330
And Hanabi did tell us to come hang out.

00:16:57.040 --> 00:16:59.330
I wanted this!

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:03.240
The more the merrier!

00:17:03.860 --> 00:17:07.060
Just don't bother the customers, please.

00:17:07.060 --> 00:17:08.330
Okay.

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:11.430
Whoa, there's so much stuff here!

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:14.220
This is my first time
at a table tennis specialty store!

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:15.890
Look at all the rubbers!

00:17:15.890 --> 00:17:18.550
Wow, so many penhold rackets!

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:21.770
Look! These number-tag pins
are really cute!

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:26.190
It's kinda nice when everyone's here, huh?

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:28.070
It's just rowdy.

00:17:29.850 --> 00:17:32.940
<i>Seriously, thanks to a certain someone,</i>

00:17:32.940 --> 00:17:35.390
<i>I never have any time to relax.</i>

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:40.530
Itsumo-san!

00:17:41.050 --> 00:17:44.970
We're going to meet up
and go shopping after stopping home.

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:46.040
Wanna come with?

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:48.660
Sorry. I'm not free today, either.

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:50.670
Busy helping out at home again?

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:51.580
Yeah.

00:17:51.580 --> 00:17:52.720
I'm really sorry.

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:53.840
Don't be.

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:55.710
Let's go some other time, then.

00:17:55.710 --> 00:17:56.480
Come on.

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:58.230
Let's go.

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:11.910
Guess who!

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:16.290
T-Tenka-san?

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:18.110
Bingo!

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:23.240
Hey, what do you rush home for every day?

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:25.080
What are you helping out with?!

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:27.140
E-Er...

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:30.570
My family runs a table tennis store.

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:32.450
I'm helping out there.

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:36.310
A store? Your family
runs a store, Itsumo-san?!

00:18:36.310 --> 00:18:37.550
Y-Yeah.

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:40.930
Wow! Having a family store sounds amazing!

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:42.260
Hey, can I come visit?

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:43.620
Can I? Can I?

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:49.000
Thank you very much.

00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:55.850
Awesome! Totally awesome!

00:18:55.850 --> 00:18:58.250
You look like this go-getter woman!

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:00.410
I-I didn't do anything special.

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:02.490
Don't get so excited.

00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:05.560
Table tennis, huh?

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:08.250
Say, is table tennis fun?

00:19:09.890 --> 00:19:12.620
I-It's really fun! Best thing in the world!

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:14.460
Best thing in the world?

00:19:15.010 --> 00:19:16.560
I see.

00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:20.530
If you're that sure, then maybe
I should try table tennis, too.

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:21.930
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:19:22.920 --> 00:19:24.760
I should get going.

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:27.680
Oh...

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:29.130
Hup.

00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:31.140
Hey, Hokuto.

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:33.930
Can I come again tomorrow?

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:37.610
<i>Did she just call me by name?</i>

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:40.310
Y-Yeah. Feel free.

00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:04.090
Thank you very much.

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:09.520
You sure have it rough,
having to help out every day.

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:10.810
I'm used to it now.

00:20:14.490 --> 00:20:17.270
I know! I'll help out with the store, too!

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:22.270
The less work you have to do,
the more we can play together!

00:20:22.270 --> 00:20:24.320
But I can't make you do that.

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:28.440
I appreciate the thought,
but you don't have to go so far.

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:31.290
What're you talking about?

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:32.750
This is nothing!

00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:36.710
I mean, we're friends!

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:55.360
I-I'm sorry! I knocked all this stuff over!

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:56.970
Are you all right?

00:20:56.970 --> 00:20:58.020
Y-Yes.

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:01.280
I'll clean this up.

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:02.830
Sorry again.

00:21:02.830 --> 00:21:05.570
Oh, don't worry about it.
They fall over all the time.

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:11.950
We'll help.

00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:21.730
Th-Thanks, you guys.
Sorry to make you do this.

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:26.630
What're you talking about? This is nothing!

00:21:26.630 --> 00:21:28.540
I mean, we're friends!

00:21:42.860 --> 00:21:43.590
Yeah...

00:21:44.290 --> 00:21:46.180
<i>Friends.</i>

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:51.330
<i>Seriously, Hanabi...</i>

00:21:56.150 --> 00:21:57.960
<i>Thanks to you,</i>

00:22:07.800 --> 00:22:10.570
<i>my life is always so rowdy.</i>

00:23:43.770 --> 00:24:00.000
Preview

00:23:45.010 --> 00:23:47.320
Your ribbon's deathly crooked.

00:23:46.330 --> 00:23:48.940
You're really clumsy,
so I'm worried to death.

00:23:48.570 --> 00:23:50.670
You weren't aware? Deathness me.

00:23:49.870 --> 00:23:52.290
First game, Tenka to serve.

00:23:52.290 --> 00:23:53.200
Love-all!

00:23:53.200 --> 00:23:54.640
Let's have a good game!

00:23:54.640 --> 00:23:57.310
Why do you play
the life-or-death game of table tennis?
